{"id":"supervision","ord":"a0","title":"The orchestrator","desc":"This subtree is the orchestrator's durable memory; the transcript is history.\n\nAt boot and after compaction, read this subtree through olai MCP → `lanes` conventions → active lane subtrees, following mirrors. Completed lanes are history, loaded only when relevant. A summary does not replace these reads.\n\nUse product docs when needed: ~/code/olai/docs/chat.md for chat/wakes and ~/code/olai/docs/format.md for addresses. Boot and rule maintenance alone do not authorize dispatch.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00","custom":{"chat-agent-session":"codex:01a08141-c109-74a3-b949-fa6723e5744d"}}
{"id":"kolu-pr-process","parent":"dag","ord":"a2","title":"Kolu exception","desc":"Kolu uses its own /be process instead of the ordinary review round. Its author opens any required paired-drishti PR. The orchestrator owns CI through odu MCP; authors do not run /ci. Merge requires /be complete and both platforms green, subject to the CI hold.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-authority","parent":"supervision","ord":"aE","title":"Authority","desc":"Execute within the human's request and approved defaults. Current explicit instructions override board defaults; higher-priority harness instructions remain binding. Ask only about consequential unresolved choices or conflicts that block an action; continue independent authorized work.\n\nPolicy changes require explicit approval. Routine memory maintenance does not. Explain process failures and propose fixes before changing policy. Keep workflow policy in this vault; product repositories supply technical conventions and build commands, while briefs govern lane process.","created":"2026-09-02T10:32:48-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-loop","parent":"supervision","ord":"aF","title":"Supervision","desc":"The human selects orchestrator/lanes.olai in terminal and CI wake pickers. Saved choices survive restart and compaction; never claim arming without evidence. Use instant kolu actions, not blocking supervision waits.\n\nOn a wake, read the lane and deepest owning step, inspect terminal/CI evidence, reconcile the lane, then advance authorized work or record a block. Re-evaluate repeated blocks; act or escalate instead of repeating acknowledgments. Dismiss events, not terminals, and never duplicate dispatch or merge.\n\nUnclaimed terminals belong to the human. Answer agent permissions only within the brief, worktree and your own authority. Report a missing scope once. Partial dispatches follow `orch-dispatch-recovery`.","created":"2026-09-02T10:32:48-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-board-rules","parent":"supervision","ord":"aEV","title":"Board and memory","desc":"Read and write .olai content through olai MCP only; git history is the read exception. Discover tool names and schemas. Report tool gaps rather than bypass validation. Follow `lanes` for board layout and commit conventions.\n\nRecord verified standing facts and approved decisions at their owning nodes, current snapshots only; git keeps history. Typed properties hold facts and claims. Read heads, CI and terminal state fresh instead of duplicating volatile progress in notes. Use `orch-standing-memory` only when no existing node owns a fact.\n\nOutstanding human decisions go in the appropriate Inbox queue as todo, linked to the owning node and PR when applicable. After resolution, record the decision at its owner and clear the queue.","created":"2026-09-02T10:32:48-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:16:00-04:00"}
{"id":"agents-root","parent":"supervision","ord":"aI","title":"Roster","desc":"Use each roster command verbatim; refuse a spawn without one. Authors run in separate kolu worktrees; terminal reviewers use splits. The choosing node owns defaults. Historical kimi observations live in orchestrator/kimi-ledger.olai.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Claude Opus","desc":"Opus with the 1M window. Verify the model at launch. Claude composer placeholders are not unsent human drafts.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"Grok","desc":"Commodity author/reviewer, especially infra and test work. Mid-turn messages queue; if still queued after submission, press Enter again. A low quota reading alone is not a reason to replace a lane; actual exhaustion is reported to the human.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"author+reviewer"}}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"Claude Fable","desc":"Use only when the human names Fable. Verify the model at launch.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-pi","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2V","title":"Pi · fallback","desc":"Fallback kimi-k3 seat (the configured default), thinking off. Shares opencode's provider pool, so switching cannot cure a pool outage. Restart corrupted sessions in the same worktree with a resume pointer.","created":"2026-08-24T16:40:49-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:16:00-04:00","custom":{"command":"pi --thinking off","role":"reviewer-fallback"}}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a5","title":"Opencode · kimi","desc":"Default commodity kimi author/reviewer. Mid-turn messages queue without interruption. Shares pi's provider pool; restart corrupted sessions in the same worktree with a resume pointer.","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00","custom":{"command":"opencode","role":"author+reviewer"}}
{"id":"roster-reviewer-contract","parent":"dag","ord":"ZzV","title":"Review contract","desc":"An independent reviewer checks the diff, surrounding invariants, acceptance criteria, behavioral tests, docs and PR claims. Check interface consistency, visible errors, dependency constraints and accidental files. The author never reviews its own lane.\n\nTests assert behavior, not styling unless styling is under test. Keep package READMEs concise, specifications in docs and marketing pages focused on the product. Prefer encapsulated components and existing SolidJS libraries; preserve Nix as the only required external dependency.\n\nReviewers read code: no suites or CI; one surgical probe is allowed. Never edit, push or merge. Terminal reviewers post one verdict with MUST/SHOULD/NIT at file:line; re-verdicts use that thread. Native assistants return evidence to the orchestrator. Add another reviewer only when justified.","created":"2026-08-26T20:09:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:16:00-04:00"}
{"id":"roster-choosing","parent":"dag","ord":"Zz","title":"Dispatch defaults","desc":"Apply defaults without repeated permission questions; record the choices before dispatch. The human's explicit choices win.\n\n- Mechanical: commodity author and one independent commodity reviewer.\n- Ordinary: commodity author and one Opus reviewer.\n- Design-heavy: Opus author for core seams, broad impact, distant invariants, no precedent or critical OS/wire assumptions; independent commodity review, adding a second reviewer for distinct expertise or risk.\n\nCommodity order: opencode; grok when occupied, unavailable or suited to infra/test mechanics; pi as fallback. Fable only by human choice. At most three concurrent Opus author lanes; reviewers do not count.\n\nDefault merge policy is merge-auto after gates pass. Honor merge-human, explicit holds and deferral approval. Trial these defaults on the next authorized bounded lane before broad roster changes.","created":"2026-08-26T20:09:47-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:16:00-04:00"}
{"id":"dag","parent":"supervision","ord":"aJ","title":"Pipeline","desc":"Before spawning, clone required steps beneath the roadmap item and place its mirror on the day board. Record author, tier, brief, worktree and merge policy. Leave execution todo until a terminal exists; then record its claim and mark item and owning step doing together. Resolve later orders from the board; partial failures follow `orch-dispatch-recovery`.\n\nNever overlap readers and writers of a worktree. At transitions, reconcile the whole lane: marks, notes, claims, mirrors and edges; compare terminal work with doing steps and repair mismatches using evidence. Omit unnecessary optional steps and reconnect dependencies. Never mark these templates.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr","parent":"dag","ord":"a0","title":"PR steps","desc":"Default PR template. The roadmap item owns lane properties; execution steps own terminal claims and relevant PR/CI properties. The day board mirrors the item.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-implement","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a0","title":"Implement and open PR","todo":true,"desc":"Brief: quote the human's request verbatim; separately state derived acceptance criteria, constraints, verified paths, validation and merge policy. Label assumptions; never invent requirements or budgets.\n\nThe author implements, runs appropriate local checks and opens a PR. Demonstrate regressions against unfixed code where reproducible; report inability honestly. Use meaningful behavior tests, not tests that mirror trivial edits.\n\nNo author merging, board writes, full CI or commissioning other terminal agents. Bound any in-session delegation. Report PR and tested revision, checks, decisions and deferrals, then stop.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-refactor","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1","title":"Refactor if needed","todo":true,"desc":"Optional: refactor material duplication or complexity with focused commits and relevant checks. Named skills and repeated passes are methods, not gates.","after":["dag-pr-implement"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge-master","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a4","title":"Merge latest master","todo":true,"desc":"After readers finish, the author merges latest master before CI using a merge commit, never a rebase. Skip empty merges; repeat only if master moves. The author resolves conflicts.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-address","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a5","title":"Address findings","todo":true,"desc":"The author addresses review findings from their comment links. Escalate findings that cannot be resolved within scope; do not silently defer them.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-ci","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a6","title":"Verify CI","todo":true,"desc":"HOLD: launch no odu run in any repo until the human lifts the 2026-09-03 hold.\n\nThe orchestrator runs CI directly through olai-plugin-odu's MCP tools, after the PR is open and review findings are folded. Missing tools are an integration block; never spawn a CI watcher. Record odu-worktree and pr-url on the CI step. The orchestrator also owns GitHub-native CI.\n\nOlai runs explicitly request platforms: [\"x86_64-linux\"]; kolu and odu need both Linux and Darwin. Read odu's operating instructions; use one venue per commit-status context. The kolu-ci pool, locked localhost (/tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock), and ci@petit are available venues; locks are per venue.\n\nRead failures yourself and route fixes to the author; rerun at the new head. CI-only fixes after review do not trigger another review unless requested. Record flakes per test file in the Inbox and handle under dispatch defaults.\n\nVerify required checks pass at the current head or mergeStateStatus is CLEAN; an agent's claim is insufficient. Open CodeQL alerts block merge.","after":["dag-pr-merge-master","dag-pr-address"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-evidence","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a7","title":"Verify evidence","todo":true,"desc":"Require evidence that proves relevant acceptance criteria. User-visible changes normally need saatchi screenshots/video against representative real data, inspected by the orchestrator. Internal/doc changes may use tests or document evidence; record why visual proof is unnecessary. Never commit proof assets to product branches.","after":["dag-pr-ci"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-deferrals","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a8","title":"Resolve deferrals","todo":true,"desc":"Unresolved deferrals require the human's explicit merge approval. Record them in the Inbox with the owning node and PR link; a follow-up instead of promised work is a deferral. Skip this gate only when none remain.","after":["dag-pr-evidence"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a9","title":"Merge","todo":true,"desc":"Read the author's final report. Squash-merge only when reviews are folded, CI passes at head, required evidence is verified and deferrals are ruled. Honor merge-human and explicit holds; unresolved work left for the human blocks merge. Admin squash-merge is allowed for an olai PR with required contexts passing.","after":["dag-pr-deferrals"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-retire","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"aA","title":"Retire terminals","todo":true,"desc":"After confirmed merge, retire all lane terminals and verify against the live list. Reviewers may retire once their verdict is folded. Partial-dispatch recovery may stop its own unclaimed new terminal earlier. Worktree removal is separate; sync the relevant checkout with git pull --ff-only.","after":["dag-pr-merge"],"created":"2026-08-17T19:20:10-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-a","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1V","title":"Review","todo":true,"desc":"Assign an independent reviewer under `roster-choosing`, following `roster-reviewer-contract`. Record reviewer and terminal claim. Mark doing before each review order; mark done only when its findings/verdict are delivered and no review work remains.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:19-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-b","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1l","title":"Second review if needed","todo":true,"desc":"Optional second reviewer for distinct expertise or material risk; same contract as the first. Remove this step and reconnect edges when unnecessary.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:25-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-timings","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"aB","title":"Record timings","todo":true,"desc":"Post one concise PR timing summary from native task spans and store it on the lane. No duplicate timing tables or manual progress ledger.","after":["dag-pr-retire"],"created":"2026-08-29T12:31:03-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-native-delegation","parent":"orch-authority","ord":"a6","title":"Native investigations","desc":"Use native Codex children for independent investigations or review assistance only when useful. Give each a bounded question, evidence requirements, deliverable and stop condition.\n\nAt most two concurrent children, subject to harness limits; no recursive delegation. Read-only by default: no board writes, durable implementation, CI, publishing or merging. The orchestrator verifies and records useful findings; the assigned reviewer owns the formal verdict.","created":"2026-09-08T09:51:47-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-dispatch-recovery","parent":"orch-loop","ord":"a3","title":"Dispatch recovery","desc":"Board preparation, terminal spawn and claim recording are separate operations. If spawning fails, leave the step todo and record the block.\n\nIf the terminal exists but its claim write fails, retain its identity for recovery and retry conditionally; never spawn a duplicate. If repair is impossible, stop only that positively identified new terminal or explicitly report why it remains running.\n\nAfter an ambiguous result or restart, identify existing terminals by worktree, branch and purpose before retrying. Never guess ownership. Reconcile the lane before more orders.","created":"2026-09-08T09:51:51-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-standing-memory","parent":"supervision","ord":"aL","title":"Standing memory","desc":"Trial the revised workflow on the next authorized bounded lane before broad roster changes. Assess interruptions, missed events, partial-dispatch recovery, review quality and time spent. No trial lane is selected.","created":"2026-09-08T09:51:56-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-codex","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a9","title":"Codex · Astra · medium","desc":"Codex with GPT-6 Astra at medium effort, specified by the human on 2026-09-08. Current orchestrator and available author/reviewer; existing dispatch defaults remain. Inherits configured permissions.\n\nDiscover actual tools and schemas; API features do not prove harness support. Mid-turn messages steer the active objective unless the human replaces it. Local chat docs describe steering and child activity cards.","created":"2026-09-08T10:05:43-04:00","changed":"2026-09-08T10:15:17-04:00","custom":{"command":"codex --model gpt-6-astra -c 'model_reasoning_effort=\"medium\"'","role":"author+reviewer"}}
